  discoveredBy: Dirk Coster
  description: Hafnium is a chemical element with symbol Hf and atomic number 72.
    A lustrous, silvery gray, tetravalent transition metal, hafnium chemically resembles
    zirconium and is found in zirconium minerals. Its existence was predicted by
    Dmitri Mendeleev in 1869, though it was not identified until 1923, making it
    the penultimate stable element to be discovered (rhenium was identified two years
    later).
